  "label": "Islamophobia: Animal Treatment Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references a common Islamophobic stereotype that Muslims are not good at treating animals, often portrayed as cruel or barbaric. This stereotype is used to create an ironic or mocking contrast with the text 'when you're a good farmer who raises healthy animals,' implying that the farmer's success is somehow unusual or exceptional for someone from a Muslim background. This stereotype is not visible in the image but is required to understand the potential underlying message or intent of the meme.",
